2 CONT This one (Forbus)is said to have a particularly strong antipathy against have had tobacco smoking, of which one still in the Area generally to tell the following event as evidence len knows. – Once when a Russian Karele was just a
2 CONC t him, one of his listeners brought him an Auer rooster to the gift. Among other questions, which of the 348 Pastor addressed him, was also the one, whether he also enjoys tobacco? As the farmer, in his simplicity, acknowledged th
2 CONC is, Forbus, in his anger, threw the rooster back at him and ordered him to immediately take it out of his sight. The Russian trader, who has such a procedure rightly seemed too strange, tried to calm the pastor 's anger and, above
2 CONC  all, to persuade him not to refuse the gift, using these words: “Take, Lord, the grouse, the grouse does not smoke tobacco”.
2 CONT
2 CONT By Mag. Zach.Forbus;, who in 1718 read the 19) S. Archbishop Tengström's treatise on the performance of the clergy in Äbo Abbey, 3rd part p. 503 ff. 20) In Kuusamo, too, according to tradition, he is said to have collected a heap 
2 CONC of the Lappish kannukset (magic drum) called by the Finns on an island in Lake Kuusamo and burned them all there.
2 CONT
